# Upstream clone + ~6.7 GB of weights + venv. Rebuild with port/README.md.
ZeroPlantSeg/

# Chunk working artifacts: commit FINDINGS.md and small figures, not bulk data.
chunks/**/*.npy
chunks/**/*.pth
chunks/**/*.ckpt
chunks/**/cache/
chunks/**/__pycache__/
chunks/**/.venv/

# A1: upstream Depth Anything 3 clone (48 MB) and the DA3 rasters it produced.
# Rebuild both with chunks/A1/README.md.
chunks/A1/da3-src/
chunks/A1/depth/*/rgb.png

*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# A2: float32 raster products (40 MB) and figures (14 MB).
# Rebuild in ~10 minutes with chunks/A2/README.md.
chunks/A2/products*/
chunks/A2/results/*.png

# A3: SAM masks, region maps and cached DINOv2 features (~100 MB).
# Rebuild in ~15 minutes with chunks/A3/README.md.
chunks/A3/work/
chunks/A3/preds/*.png
chunks/A3/figs/*.png

# A4: fragment maps, cached graph, cached A3 material, and the unresolved-edge
# lists (3.3 MB each). Rebuild in ~3.5 min with chunks/A4/README.md.
chunks/A4/work/
chunks/A4/figs/*.png
chunks/A4/products/*.png
chunks/A4/products/unresolved_edges_*.json

# A5: figures (13 MB). Rebuild in ~30 s with chunks/A5/figures.py.
chunks/A5/figs/*.png

# A6: the voxel keep-out product (7.9 MB) and figures (9.3 MB).
# Rebuild in ~5 min with chunks/A6/README.md.
chunks/A6/products/*.npz
chunks/A6/figs/*.png

# A7: the stimulus PNGs (418 MB) and the figures (2.7 MB).
# Rebuild the renders in ~4 min with `run_a7.py render`; the replies cost $41
# and cannot be regenerated identically, so they are kept OUT of the ignore
# list deliberately — see the note below.
chunks/A7/renders/
chunks/A7/work/
chunks/A7/figs/*.png

# A8: the keep-out distance table (350 KB) and the figures (3.3 MB), plus the
# client-only venv holding `mcp` for the conformance check. Rebuild the
# products in ~40 s with `chunks/A8/build_products.py` and the figures in ~10 s
# with `chunks/A8/figures.py`; recreate the venv with the two commands at the
# top of `chunks/A8/requirements-client.lock.txt`. The JSON products and
# everything in chunks/A8/results/ are kept: they are the chunk's evidence.
chunks/A8/products/*.npz
chunks/A8/figs/*.png
chunks/A8/.venv-client/

# A1b: one complete set of A2 + A4 products per assumed focal length, twice
# over (seeded and free-seed sweeps) — ~900 MB. Rebuild in ~90 min with
# chunks/A1b/sweep_all.sh; every number derived from it is in
# chunks/A1b/results/*.json, which ARE committed.
chunks/A1b/work/
chunks/A1b/figs/*.png
